#
# Counter-example for math:RingDistributivityShape: a math:Ring that declares its carrier,
# both operations, and an axiom, but omits math:satisfiesDistributivity (sh:minCount 1) —
# two operations with no law tying them together are two unrelated groups, not a ring. It
# satisfies math:AlgebraicStructureShape (carrier + operation + an axiom), so validation
# MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and no other finding (math:NonDistributiveRing).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecRingMissingDistributivity).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:nonDistributiveRing a math:Ring ;
    math:underlyingSet ex:ringCarrier ;
    math:structureOperation ex:ringAdd , ex:ringMul ;
    math:satisfiesAxiom ex:ringAssoc .

ex:ringCarrier a math:Set .
ex:ringAdd a math:Operation .
ex:ringMul a math:Operation .
ex:ringAssoc a math:Axiom .
